        "lang": "en",
        "note_tweet": {
          "text": "DAILY AI BRIEF 🗞 — Nov 16\n\nALIBABA 🔥:\n- Qwen4-Max is out, a 2.4T MoE model with native vision and 1M context at $1.50/$4.50 per 1M tokens.\n\nTENCENT 🔥:\n- Tencent launched Hy4 Flash, a 1M-context multimodal model at $0.07/$0.281 per 1M tokens, with 50% off through November 30.\n\nOPENAI 🔥:\n- OpenAI is testing a new ChatGPT web interface on desktop with cards for content creation and activities (via oncescuradu).\n\nGOOGLE 🔥:\n- Antigravity is doubling the context window for Gemini 4 Argon, Carbon and Hydrogen.\n- An upcoming Comic artifact in Gemini Notebook now shows style examples.\n\nMETA 🔥:\n- Meta opened a waitlist for Muse Hatch in the US.\n\nAPPLE 🔥:\n- Siri AI app integrations will be the centerpiece of Apple's smart glasses next year, per Bloomberg.\n\nNVIDIA 🔥:\n- Jensen Huang is reportedly considering a return as NVIDIA CEO, per the FT.\n\n* Used Grok to compose this brief, cherry-picking the news and doing some post-editing."
